> ec y^2 = x^3 + 1 mod 7
y^2 = x^3 + 1 over F_7
  curve: y^2 = x^3 + 1 over F_7
  discriminant: 2
  j: 0
  order: #E = 12
  factored: 2^2 * 3
  trace: -4
  how: naive: 1 + sum over x of (1 + (x^3 + ax + b | p)), with a table of squares
  check: N = 12 is the only multiple of 12 in the Hasse interval [3, 13]
  supersingular: no (t != 0 mod p)
  group: Z/6 x Z/2
  check: P1 = (4, 3) has order n1; R = (2, 4); the Weil pairing e_n1(P1, R) = 6 has order n2, so <P1, R> has at least n1 n2 = #E points
  twist order: 4
  embedding degree: 1 (of r = 3: r | p^1 - 1)
